<anchor xml:id="_class_command_runner_1ab280bbfaeb4950d2543ce1b649454bec"/><section>
    <title>background()</title>
<indexterm><primary>background</primary><secondary>CommandRunner</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>CommandRunner</primary><secondary>background</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput>background (string $command)<computeroutput>[static]</computeroutput></computeroutput></para>
<para>Launch a command in the background without waiting for output.</para>

<para>Uses the Windows &quot;start /B&quot; cmd.exe idiom to detach the process immediately. The caller is responsible for ensuring $command is properly constructed; use escapeshellarg() on any dynamic values before passing them in.</para>

