<anchor xml:id="_class_command_runner_1a915d51b1a5c695e480f65ed3984adb86"/><section>
    <title>stream()</title>
<indexterm><primary>stream</primary><secondary>CommandRunner</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>CommandRunner</primary><secondary>stream</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput>stream (string $executable, array $args, callable $lineCallback)<computeroutput>[static]</computeroutput></computeroutput></para>
<para>Execute an executable with arguments, streaming output line-by-line.</para>

<para>Useful for long-running processes that emit progress information. Each argument is individually escaped with escapeshellarg(). Lines are split on carriage-return (\r) to match Windows progress-reporting conventions. Any data remaining in the buffer after EOF is flushed as a final line.</para>

<para>
